)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Messages -- A to C                       !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}  The messages of the title line, A to Z; n is a number, x a string.
@"O" ACTION REQUIRED
}    H: a new DEST goes only with O in the NP column, which releases it.
@ACTION NOT AVAILABLE YET
}    The action character is one of the Status panel's, but this panel does
}    not take it yet. Use it on ST.
@ACTION=ALL, ACTION=OFF, ACTION=1,2,...
}    What ACTION has now set: which replies are shown at the end of the log.
@BOTTOM OF DATA REACHED
}    FIND went to the end without finding the string again. The next FIND
}    starts over at the top.
@CANNOT CANCEL THIS JOB
}    JES2 would not cancel the job for P.
@CHARS 'x' FOUND}  (or WORD, PREFIX, SUFFIX)    @n CHARS 'x' FOUND
}    FIND found the string; with ALL, in n lines.
@COMMAND ISSUED
}    SDSF gave the JES2 or operator command. The answer is in the log.
@COMMAND NOT AUTHORIZED
}    SDSF could not get the authorized state for the command (topic 13 of
}    the contents), or LOG, PR or INIT without READ access to SDSF.OPER.
}
}  Enter: next page   PF7: contents   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHMS2
  &ZUP = ISFHTOC
)END
